BT /F1 11 Tf 56 742.0 Td (Neural Networks - Lecture Notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 727.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 713.0 Td (Course: Introduction to Machine Learning \(Lecture 4\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 698.5 Td (Topic: Feedforward networks, training, and modern architectures) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 684.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 669.5 Td (1. What is a neural network?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 655.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 640.5 Td (A neural network is a parameterised function that maps an input vector x to an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 626.0 Td (output vector y through a sequence of layers. Each layer applies a linear) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 611.5 Td (transformation followed by a non-linear activation:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 597.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 582.5 Td (  z = W x + b) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 568.0 Td (  a = f\(z\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 553.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 539.0 Td (where W is a weight matrix, b is a bias vector, and f is an element-wise) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 524.5 Td (activation function. A network with one hidden layer can approximate any) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 510.0 Td (continuous function on a bounded domain \(universal approximation theorem\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 495.5 Td (but depth usually buys far more representational power per parameter than) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 481.0 Td (width.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 466.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 452.0 Td (The learnable parameters are exactly the entries of every W and b. Training) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 437.5 Td (means finding values for these parameters that minimise a loss on the training) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 423.0 Td (data while generalising to unseen data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 408.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 394.0 Td (2. The forward pass) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 379.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 365.0 Td (The forward pass evaluates the network from input to output. For a two-layer) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 350.5 Td (network:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 336.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 321.5 Td (  h = f\(W1 x + b1\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 307.0 Td (  y_hat = softmax\(W2 h + b2\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 292.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 278.0 Td (The intermediate vectors h are called activations or hidden representations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 263.5 Td (A useful mental model: each layer learns a new coordinate system in which the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 249.0 Td (task becomes easier - early layers detect local patterns, deeper layers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 234.5 Td (compose them into abstract concepts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 220.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 205.5 Td (3. Activation functions) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 191.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 176.5 Td (- Sigmoid: sigma\(z\) = 1 / \(1 + e^-z\). Output in \(0,1\). Saturates for large) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 162.0 Td (  |z|, so gradients vanish; rarely used in hidden layers today.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 147.5 Td (- Tanh: zero-centred version of sigmoid, still saturating.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 133.0 Td (- ReLU: max\(0, z\). Cheap, sparse, and the default for most feedforward and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 118.5 Td (  convolutional networks. Dying ReLU is its main failure mode \(neurons stuck) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 104.0 Td (  at zero\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 89.5 Td (- Leaky ReLU / GELU / SiLU: smooth or leaky variants that mitigate dead units) Tj ET
endstream
