BT /F1 11 Tf 56 742.0 Td (- Learning rate is the single most important hyperparameter. Too large and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 727.5 Td (  loss diverges; too small and training stalls. Schedules \(cosine decay,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 713.0 Td (  warm-up\) usually help.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 698.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 684.0 Td (7. Regularisation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 669.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 655.0 Td (- Weight decay \(L2\) penalises large weights and shrinks the effective capacity) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 640.5 Td (  of the model.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 626.0 Td (- Dropout randomly zeroes activations during training, forcing redundant and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 611.5 Td (  robust representations. Disable it at inference time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 597.0 Td (- Early stopping halts training when validation loss stops improving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 582.5 Td (- Data augmentation \(crops, flips, noise\) expands the effective dataset.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 568.0 Td (- Batch normalisation stabilises activations and often allows higher learning) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 553.5 Td (  rates.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 539.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 524.5 Td (8. Modern architectures) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 510.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 495.5 Td (- Convolutional networks \(CNNs\) exploit spatial locality with shared filters;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 481.0 Td (  pooling reduces resolution. They dominate vision.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 466.5 Td (- Recurrent networks \(RNNs, LSTMs\) process sequences with a hidden state, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 452.0 Td (  suffer from vanishing gradients over long spans.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 437.5 Td (- Transformers replace recurrence with self-attention, allowing every position) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 423.0 Td (  to attend to every other in parallel. Attention weights are learned) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 408.5 Td (  similarities; multi-head attention lets the model attend to several) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 394.0 Td (  relationships at once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 379.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 365.0 Td (9. Common pitfalls) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 350.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 336.0 Td (- Overfitting: training loss falls while validation loss rises. Fix with more) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 321.5 Td (  data, regularisation, or a smaller model.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 307.0 Td (- Vanishing / exploding gradients: caused by repeated multiplication of small) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 292.5 Td (  or large Jacobians. Mitigate with ReLU, residual connections, or gradient) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 278.0 Td (  clipping.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 263.5 Td (- Data leakage: information from the validation set sneaks into training) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 249.0 Td (  \(e.g. normalising before splitting\). Always split first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 234.5 Td (- Imbalanced classes: accuracy is misleading when one class dominates. Use) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 220.0 Td (  precision, recall, F1, or resample.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 205.5 Td (- Not shuffling: correlated batches bias the gradient estimate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 191.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 176.5 Td (10. Key formulas) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 162.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 147.5 Td (  forward:        a = f\(W x + b\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 133.0 Td (  loss \(CE\):      L = -sum y * log\(y_hat\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 118.5 Td (  update:         theta <- theta - lr * dL/dtheta) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 104.0 Td (  chain rule:     dL/dx = \(dL/df\)\(df/dg\)...\(dh/dx\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 89.5 Td (  ReLU:           f\(z\) = max\(0, z\)) Tj ET
endstream
